<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43517" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sēmĭnātor</span></b> ,
			ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an originator</i>, <i>producer</i>, <i>author</i> (Ciceronian). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">seminator et sator et parens omnium rerum
					(mundus),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 2, 34, 86</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnium malorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 3, 26, 66</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tamquam fallaciae seminatores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 5, 2, 17</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
